Schéma v1 (à coller dans l’API / Zod). Je ne peux pas l’écrire dans le repo en Ask mode.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "portco-brief-v1",
  "title": "PortcoBrief",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schemaVersion",
    "orgId",
    "title",
    "headline",
    "leadershipSnapshot",
    "strengths",
    "risks",
    "gaps",
    "flags",
    "suggestedActions",
    "sourceDocumentIds"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schemaVersion": {
      "const": "portco-brief-v1"
    },
    "orgId": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["PC1", "PC2", "PC3"]
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "e.g. Cascade Care Group — leadership brief"
    },
    "headline": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "2–4 sentences Dana can read in one breath. No claim without citationIds on the supporting arrays."
    },
    "leadershipSnapshot": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/seatRead" }
    },
    "strengths": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/claim" }
    },
    "risks": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/claim" }
    },
    "gaps": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/gap" },
      "description": "What the corpus does not support. Prefer this over inventing a claim."
    },
    "flags": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/flag" }
    },
    "suggestedActions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/action" }
    },
    "sourceDocumentIds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string", "format": "uuid" },
      "description": "Documents actually used (subset of retrieved set)."
    }
  },
  "$defs": {
    "chunkId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Must be one of the chunk ids provided in the prompt."
    },
    "claim": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["text", "citationIds"],
      "properties": {
        "text": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
        "citationIds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/chunkId" },
          "minItems": 1
        }
      }
    },
    "seatRead": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["seat", "summary", "citationIds"],
      "properties": {
        "seat": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "CEO, CFO, COO, … as named in sources"
        },
        "personName": { "type": "string" },
        "summary": { "type": "string" },
        "signal": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": ["green", "yellow", "red", "unknown"]
        },
        "citationIds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/chunkId" },
          "minItems": 1
        }
      }
    },
    "gap": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["text"],
      "properties": {
        "text": { "type": "string" },
        "relatedSeat": { "type": "string" }
      }
    },
    "flag": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["code", "text"],
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "single_source",
            "contradiction",
            "thin_evidence",
            "stale_source"
          ]
        },
        "text": { "type": "string" },
        "citationIds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/chunkId" }
        }
      }
    },
    "action": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["text"],
      "properties": {
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Suggested next step, not a decision. Must not invent facts."
        },
        "citationIds": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/chunkId" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Post-LLM (code, pas Claude) :** tout `citationId` ∉ chunks envoyés → claim viré ou passé en `gaps` ; `flags` `single_source` si `citationIds.length === 1`.  
**Pas dans ce JSON :** `generatedAt`, `conversationId`, `promptVersion` — colonnes SQL.

Équivalent Zod à coller dans l’API si tu préfères ça au JSON Schema fichier. Passe en Agent mode si tu veux que je l’ajoute au repo.

Ce n’est **pas** un 4ᵉ service Docker. C’est un **petit dossier de code Node** importé par l’API **et** le worker, pour ne pas copier-coller MiniLM.

**Pourquoi `embed/` :** c’est là que vit `embed(text) → number[384]`. Tu pourrais l’appeler `embeddings/` ou `vector/`. Le nom décrit **la fonction**, pas un produit Xenova.

```
packages/embed/
  package.json          name: "@secondbrain/embed"
  src/index.ts          pipeline MiniLM, export embed()
```

```ts
// packages/embed/src/index.ts
import { pipeline } from '@xenova/transformers';

const extractor = await pipeline(
  'feature-extraction',
  'Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2'
);

export async function embed(text: string): Promise<number[]> {
  const out = await extractor(text, { pooling: 'mean', normalize: true });
  return Array.from(out.data);
}
```

- **Worker** : `embed(chunk)` → INSERT  
- **API** : `embed(question)` → `ORDER BY embedding <=> $q`  

**Même modèle, même dim.** Sinon retrieve cassé.

---

**Optionnel** vraiment : si `apps/api` et `apps/worker` sont **le même package** Node (`src/embed.ts` + deux entrypoints), tu **n’as pas** besoin de `packages/embed`. Un workspace npm n’existe que pour partager sans dupliquer.

Pour 2–3 h : **un backend, deux commandes**, `embed.ts` à côté. `packages/embed` = si tu tiens à deux apps séparées.
